-- NEWER VGM SEGA/Atlus — Section 10 part A (Jet Set Radio + E3 Prototype)
--
-- Source: reference/NEWER VGM Sound Sources - SEGAAtlus.csv lines 1356-1581.
-- 2 game records, ~219 usage rows. Section 10 split into 10a / 10b — JSR
-- Future has its own seed file due to total section size.
--
-- Jet Set Radio E3 Prototype (April 2000) split into its own game record
-- per the HotD Arcade Prototype / Puyo Puyo Sun split convention. The CSV
-- identifies a distinct prototype build with samples (Beastie Boys,
-- fIREHOSE) and synth gear (KORG MS-20, Roland System-100M) seen on the
-- "Holiday Plug-In!" promotional cover.
--
-- Verbatim preservations (Rule 2):
--   - Dual JP/Western title "Jet Set Radio / Jet Grind Radio".
--   - "Sample: Miles Davis - High Speed Chase" (T1376) — same Miles Davis
--     track sampled by SEGA Rally 2 in Section 5. Cross-game sample reuse.
--   - "Live Recording: B.B. Rights/Billy Brown (Vocals)" + F-Fields
--     (Electric Guitar) — the iconic "Jet Set Radio!" station IDs.
--   - "DJ Toolz / Break Beats 'N' Grooves Vol. 3" preserved distinct
--     from "Ninja Tune / Break Beats 'N' Grooves Volume Three" — possibly
--     same library but different publisher attributions in CSV.
--   - "KORG / TRINITY proX" — new variant joining TRINITY and TRINITY pro
--     in the DB.
--   - E3 build "(Fuzita Blender)" parenthetical examples preserved as-is.

